are taken verbatim from kiddin9/op-packages at commit
19a44706dde7554f21c9d0503cdcfc399914067f, directory `luci-app-quickstart/`.
That repository is distributed under the GNU General Public License v2.0
(see its LICENSE file); `istore_backend.lua` carries its own MIT header and
`luci-app-quickstart/Makefile` in that repository claims Apache-2.0, so the
combined package is published as GPL-2.0-only, the strictest of the three.

The static web assets are NOT taken from that repository: they are installed
from the official istoreos/quickstart release archive, which is MIT licensed,
so the assets and the quickstart binary always share one release.
